% holding-decision: considering
% holding-decision-note: Held as a link only (README, "Cultures that protect their music"): MusiCounts gives the scores free as "open-access", but nothing printed on the scores or the site licenses reposting them, so no notation or audio is kept here.
% holding-blocked: Still needed: Sherryl Sewepagaham's written permission (and MusiCounts', who host the scores) before any notation is posted on the site; and a review by the TDSB Urban Indigenous Education Centre or by the composer of the credit, the story and how the class sings it. Neither has happened. Until then students use the MusiCounts page itself.
% holding-kind: link
% holding-kind-note: No notes or words by design: the composer and MusiCounts share the four scores and the pronunciation guide on their own page, and their terms do not say others may repost them. Link to musicounts.ca/en/miteh.
% source-url: https://musicounts.ca/en/miteh/ MusiCounts page: "A new, open-access choral work by Sherryl Sewepagaham"; four free scores, pronunciation guide and instructional video
